## Description

This detection identifies the execution of **Windows Scheduled Tasks (schtasks.exe)** using **Microsoft Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation)**.

Windows Task Scheduler allows users and administrators to automate program execution based on specific triggers. Threat actors frequently abuse scheduled tasks to establish persistence, execute malware, or maintain access after compromising a system.

Monitoring `schtasks.exe` execution enables defenders to detect suspicious persistence mechanisms and unauthorized task creation.

